\begin_layout Section
North Ameican Black and White Television (For Historical Purposes)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The picture is divided into 525 lines,
 which constitute a frame.Each frame is decomposed into two interlaced fields,
 each of which consits of 262.5 lines.For convenience of presentation,
 we will we will refer to the two fields as I and II.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename Images/Engeneering/EE/Communication Engineering/ReducedSize/B&WRaster.jpg

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The time taken for each field to be scanned is 1/60 s .Correspondingly the time taken for a frame or a complete picture to be scanned is 1/30 s.
 With 525 lines in a frame ,
 the line scanning frequency is 15.75 kHz.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus ,
 by flashing 30 still pictures per second on the display tube of the TV receiver,
 the human eye perceives them to be moving pictures.
\end_layout

